<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">St. Panteleimon Monastery</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rossikon, Russian monastery of Mount Athos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">St. Panteleimon Monastery, known as the Rossikon, is the Russian monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-athos">Mount Athos</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. Russian monks are recorded on Athos from the 11th century, and the present monastery on the coast was built mainly in the 19th century, when Russian support made it home to more than a thousand monks. It declined after the Russian Revolution but has revived since the 1990s with renewed ties to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/st-panteleimon-monastery.jpg" alt="St. Panteleimon Monastery" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kremlin.ru · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rossikon_%E2%80%93_the_St_Panteleimon_Monastery_on_Mount_Athos_%C2%B7_2016_%C2%B7_Image_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
